{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/223898-exalted-copyright-question","id":223898,"title":"Exalted copyright question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-09T23:12:47-07:00","id":223898,"title":"Exalted copyright question","content":"So, a couple friends of mine decided that they want to try writing a short, 5 or 6 hour visual novel (a couple of them are artists, two of them are writers and one enjoys making music), and they were thinking of having the story take place in the Exalted setting. <br /> <br /> But, before they run off making something, I thought I'd ask what the policy for that might be. My friends are of the opinion that it's no different from a web comic or a fan-fiction story, though since it is a different type of media, I thought it would be better to ask than be sorry, especially with the slightly weird place Exalted (and the other stuff White Wolf stuff) is in now - owned by CCP but licensed to Onyx Path. <br /> <br /> For people unfamiliar with them, visual novels are basically stories with character portraits, backgrounds and music, usually with little to no gameplay other than choices you can select to take the story in different directions (but sometimes you don't even have those and the story runs just like a book novel).<br /> <br /> So would that be okay or would they be likely to run into copyright issues if people at CCP felt it was too close to a &quot;game?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T02:44:14-07:00","id":223985,"